# THE FITTED COEFFICIENT LAYER  (PLAN D2a)
# ==========================================================================
#
# Six per-layer profiles, each a 4-knot monotone cubic (PCHIP) over the layer
# index, exported as `_COEFFS` so `tools/fit.py` can rewrite them and re-emit a
# single frozen file.
#
# EVERY PROFILE IS A MULTIPLIER WITH DEFAULT 1.0, never a replacement for the
# frozen constant it scales. That is not a stylistic choice: `_K4_LAM` is a
# 16-entry table that is NOT smooth, and a 4-knot spline fitted through it
# misses by 6.4e-03 against a table whose whole range is 9.8e-03 (measured,
# `tools/_pchip4_check.py`). Replacing the table with a spline would therefore
# change the estimator at its own defaults, and bit-parity with C10 -- the thing
# that makes a fitted result attributable -- would be unreachable. As
# multipliers, `None` and `[1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0]` are both exactly the identity.
#
# The profiles are evaluated on PYTHON SCALARS, once per layer, so they issue no
# flopscope operations at all: the coefficient layer is free at runtime and
# cannot move the FLOP or op count. Verified by a cost run against C10.
